{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And this is the Torah which Moses set.</b> These are the commandments that he will mention immediately after this parashah." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״וזאת התורה״ — this is added to the cities of refuge: just as the cities of refuge deliver from death, so too does the Torah; and not only that, but it delivers more than the cities of refuge, for the cities of refuge receive only inadvertent killers, whereas the Torah receives both inadvertent and deliberate. Israel said to Moses: If the cities of refuge were annulled, where would we flee? He said to them: to the Torah, as it says, ״וזאת התורה״. This is what is written (Proverbs 3:18): ״עץ חיים היא למחזיקים בה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:39.542795597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}